    'NO Update 090. NO Update 091. NO VRA Overview No. 4. NO Warning 121-26. All four were probed by DIRECT FILE URL under multiple date and suffix variants and all returned empty, so these are retrieval results against the working method rather than assumptions. Update 089 (ICOD 251500Z) therefore stands as the live instrument: cumulative confirmed vessel incidents since 1 March 96, two since the prior report; Regional Threat Level SEVERE; Strait of Hormuz SEVERE — “deliberate hostile action considered as highly likely”; Gulf of Oman MODERATE (the reclassification of the Musandam-area strikes into the Hormuz bucket, not a de-escalation); Arabian Gulf MODERATE; Gulf of Aden and Bab el-Mandeb SUBSTANTIAL. Verbatim on mines, and note the PAST TENSE of the original, which describes the reporting period to ICOD 251500Z: “There remained a continued risk of drifting or uncharted mines in and near the TSS, with mine danger areas still active.” Clearance and survey operations continue and coordinates are held by NAVCENT NCAGS. Six merchant vessels remain held. EPOCH NOTE: UKMTO counts from 1 March, Windward from 28 February and this document’s market anchor is the 27 February close — three start dates, each on its own provider’s basis, never to be differenced.',
