   ['WASHINGTON — no timetable, and no sanctions action',
    'Trump to Al Jazeera, 26 August: “I have no time schedule, none. I’m not in a hurry.” That is the clearest statement this monitor has recorded that no US–Iran talks are scheduled, and it cuts both ways: a frozen track is neither escalation nor resolution. US–IRAN TALKS NOT RESUMED AND NONE SCHEDULED. NO OFAC IRAN ACTION on 26 or 27 August — both treasury.gov press releases and OFAC Recent Actions read live. The financial-institution designation Bessent signalled “before end of week” has NOT issued and NO CHINESE BANK is designated; AP reporting of 26 August cites the September Xi state visit as the constraint. The operative notice remains the five E.O. 13902 sector determinations effective 24 August, with a wind-down to 8 September. Axios (25 August, two unnamed officials): Secretary Rubio told allied foreign ministers the US expects no new strikes on Iran “for the time being”, possibly until after the November midterms — NO confirmation or denial from State, the Department of War or the White House could be sourced through the cutoff, so it CORROBORATES the observed silence rather than establishing a policy.',
    'Al Jazeera interview 26 Aug (Tier 1); treasury.gov and OFAC Recent Actions read live 27 Aug (Tier 1); AP via Fortune 26 Aug; Axios 25 Aug (Tier 2, two unnamed officials).'],
   ['THE REGION AND TEHRAN’S DOMESTIC TRANSMISSION',
    'Qatar’s prime minister telephoned BOTH foreign ministers on 25 August and Al Ansari says officials are on the phone daily. NO Pakistan follow-up after Field Marshal Munir’s 24 August Tehran visit. The UAE embargo of 19 August STILL has no published implementing decree, carve-out, licence regime or CBUAE circular — EIGHT DAYS on. Iran: the Hormuz transit-fee article is NOT ENACTED — it cleared the National Security and Foreign Policy Committee on 23 August and requires a full-parliament vote and Guardian Council review, and no plenary vote was reported on 26 or 27 August. The PGSA non-compliant vessel list is reported at 46 ships by gCaptain and 45 tankers by Reuters — two counts on different units, neither reconciled. SNSC Secretary Mohsen Rezaei made NO public intervention at all in the window and the file has visibly moved from the Supreme National Security Council to the foreign ministry; his 24 August naming of Saudi and Emirati bypass pipelines as targets is unretracted and remains single-stream Tier 3, and is NOT used to move a probability. Domestic transmission, carried as context and NOT used to move a probability: the rial touched a record 2,060,000 to the dollar intraday against an official CBI rate near 1.5 mn, inflation runs near 90% on the Statistical Centre of Iran’s own figure, and a petrol shortage is reported at roughly 135 mn litres a day of consumption against about 121 mn of output, with overnight queues and the government signalling a price rise and rationing within weeks. Petrol pricing is the precise trigger of the November 2019 protests, so this is a live domestic-instability channel — recorded, and deliberately not scored on single-stream sourcing. NO new IAEA statement on Iran. NO Houthi or Red Sea attack on 26 or 27 August.',
    'The Peninsula 25–26 Aug on Qatar; wam.ae and CBUAE checked for an implementing decree (confirmed negative); Iranian domestic economic reporting (Tier 2/Tier 3); gCaptain and Reuters on the PGSA list.'],
